 61V  c  2020Mi13: E=345 MeV/nucleon {+70}Zn beam was produced from the I|g Beam
 61V 2c  Factory (RIBF) at RIKEN. Target was 2.2 g/cm{+2} {+9}Be. Fragments     
 61V 3c  were separated and identified by the time-of-flight magnetic-rigidity  
 61V 4c  (tof-B|r) method and energy-loss using the BigRIPS separator, the      
 61V 5c  SHARAQ spectrometer, CVD diamond and silicon strip detectors. |g rays  
 61V 6c  were detected with a detection system consisting with a plastic        
 61V 7c  stopper, twp HPGe clover detectors and a plastic veto detector.        
